 14C7 32        		DB	50		;GAP3MPM II V2.1 file explanation.                Nov 2,1982

	The file named BNKXIOS.ASM is the MPM II V2.1 banked XIOS module.
In the front of this file is a series of Equates which you must set for
your situation. This module only supports 1 extra console and therefore
you will have to add additional console and printer drivers as needed in
your case.

	After you have edited your changes, the next step is to assemble
the bnkxios file as follows:

	RMAC BNKXIOS {$options in MAC manual}

	After the assembly process is complete, you must next LINK the
file into a BNKXIOS.SPR file for the gensys process.

	LINK BNKXIOS [os]

	This completes the generation if the bnkxios file.


	The file named LDRBIOS.ASM is the primary loader module for the
MPMLDR.COM file. This file must be assembled using MAC from Digital
Research.
	Edit and make changes to the file as needed for your situation.
If you need to initialize additional I/O devices, this is the module in
which to do it in. Initialization is all done in the routine called INIT:

	After your editing is complete, assemble the file as follows:

	MAC LDRBIOS {$options as in MAC manual}

	After the assembly, the file must next be overlayed into the
MPMLDR.COM file as follows:

	DDT MPMLDR.COM
	next    pc
	xxxx	xxxx
	-ILDRBIOS.HEX		;file to load
	-R			;read in ldrbios.hex file
	-^C			;exit back to system
A>SAVE 28 XMPMLDR.COM<cr>	;save the new loader module

	You are now ready to try to boot up MPM. Besure to read the MPM
manuals real well.
